data: {"text":"Whirlpool says top-load filters usually aren't user-accessible, so I'll put together a safe plan with the simple checks you can do first.","type":"say"}

data: {"plan":{"appliance":"top-load washer","brand":"Whirlpool","diagnosis":"Water stays because the lid, load, or drain path may be stopping the spin and drain. Top-load Whirlpool washers usually do not have a filter you can clean yourself, so stop and call a pro if simple checks fail.","library_id":"","library_problem":"","manual_url":"https://www.whirlpool.com/blog/washers-and-dryers/why-is-my-washing-machine-not-draining.html","model_number":"","replacement_parts":[],"safety":["Unplug the washer before reaching inside or moving hoses.","Do not remove panels or open the pump — call a pro for that.","Mop up spilled water quickly to avoid slipping."],"steps":[{"check":"The washer is unplugged and the plug is visible.","details":["This makes it safe to reach in.","Leave it unplugged for the next checks."],"instruction":"Unplug the washer from the wall","motion":"pull_out","photo":-1,"show_3d":false,"target_part":"power plug"},{"check":"No water is scooped into the drum; the bucket holds it.","details":["Use a cup to lower the water level.","This makes moving wet clothes easier."],"instruction":"Scoop standing water into a bucket","motion":"none","photo":-1,"show_3d":false,"target_part":"standing water in tub"},{"check":"The lid sits fully closed with no clothes trapped.","details":["An open lid can stop drain and spin.","Push down gently until it feels shut."],"instruction":"Close the lid fully and firmly","motion":"push_in","photo":-1,"show_3d":true,"target_part":"washer lid"},{"check":"Clothes form a loose, even ring in the tub.","details":["Spread clothes around, not in one clump.","Remove one bulky item if the tub is packed."],"instruction":"Spread wet clothes evenly around tub","motion":"none","photo":-1,"show_3d":false,"target_part":"wet clothes in tub"},{"check":"The drain hose lies smooth, with no sharp bends.","details":["Look behind the washer without pulling it far.","Do not disconnect the hose.","If you cannot see it easily, skip this check."],"instruction":"Check drain hose for kinks behind washer","motion":"none","photo":-1,"show_3d":true,"target_part":"drain hose behind washer"},{"check":"Water leaves the tub, or you stop and call a pro.","details":["Plug in, close lid, choose Drain \u0026 Spin.","Stay nearby and listen for draining.","If water stays or you hear loud humming, unplug and call a pro."],"instruction":"Run Drain and Spin once","motion":"press","photo":-1,"show_3d":false,"target_part":"Drain and Spin cycle setting"}],"tools":["bucket","cup","towels"]},"type":"plan"}

